<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">and similarly we can define <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda),Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,-}_{G,v,u}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda),Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-,+}_{G,v,u}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda),Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+,-}_{G,v,u}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda),Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-,+}_{G,v,u}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-,-}_{G,v,u}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>u</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-,-}_{G,v,u}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math> If <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is already pinned in <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> (for example to <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math>), then automatically <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda).</annotation></semantics></math>
Given a partial configuration <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, for any <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{\prime}\subset\Lambda," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{\prime}\subset\Lambda,</annotation></semantics></math> we denote <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> the restriction of <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, called a sub-partial configuration of <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Consider the rational function <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=\frac{Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)}{Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=\frac{Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)}{Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)}.</annotation></semantics></math>
Note that when <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\gamma,\lambda{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\gamma,\lambda{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the marginal probability of <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> being assigned to the spin <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> in the Gibbs distribution.
However, when <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\gamma,\lambda\in\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\gamma,\lambda\in\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> has no probabilistic meaning and <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\in\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\in\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the setting <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>,
there are trivial partial configurations such that
<math id="S2.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,v}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We rule these cases out as they are <em id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">infeasible</em>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 5</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Feasible partial configuration)<span id="Thmtheorem5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Given a 2-spin system defined on a graph <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>,
a partial configuration <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible if
<math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> does not assign any two adjacent vertices in <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> both to the spin <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> does not assign any two adjacent vertices in <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> both to the spin <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We say a vertex <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math> is proper to a feasible partial configuration <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> if <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\notin\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\notin\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> and the partial configurations <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{+}_{\Lambda\cup\{v\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{+}_{\Lambda\cup\{v\}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{-}_{\Lambda\cup\{v\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{-}_{\Lambda\cup\{v\}}</annotation></semantics></math>
obtained from <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> by further pinning <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem5.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>−</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-</annotation></semantics></math> respectively are still feasible.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Any sub-partial configuration of a feasible partial configuration is still feasible.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem6" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 6</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Zero-freeness)<span id="Thmtheorem6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}\subseteq\mathbb{C}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐔</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}\subseteq\mathbb{C}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be a family of graphs. The partition function of the 2-spin systems defined on <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> is said to be <em id="Thmtheorem6.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">zero-free</em> on <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐔</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> if for any graph <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, any feasible partial configuration <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="Thmtheorem6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\in\mathbf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>𝐔</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)\in\mathbf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">When the parameters <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> of a 2-spin system are fixed,
we may write the partition function <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and the rational function <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, which are both univariate functions on <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
Sometimes we may omit the fixed parameters <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> at the subscript for simplicity.
The definition of zero-freeness can be easily adopted to the partition function <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and similarly to <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\gamma,\lambda}(\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\gamma,\lambda}(\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\lambda}(\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\lambda}(\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math> with fixed <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.
When the three parameters are all fixed, we may write the value <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and the value <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S2.SS1.p3.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> for simplicity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Suppose that the partition function <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-free on some <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subseteq\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>U</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subseteq\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then, the rational function <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic on <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> for any graph <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and any feasible partial configuration <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Moreover, if the vertex <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is proper to <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> or <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}(\lambda)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">+</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},+}(\lambda)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}(\lambda)\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},-}(\lambda)\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>.
Notice that <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\lambda\rightarrow 0}P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\lambda\rightarrow 0}P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
We agree that <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)=0</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the zero-free region <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> is of the form <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0)\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.222em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0)\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math> for some complex neighbourhood <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0)</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>,
then the rational function <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,\beta,\gamma,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is analytic on the entire <math id="S2.SS1.p4.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{N}(0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{N}(0)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem7" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 7</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Strong spatial mixing)<span id="Thmtheorem7.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem7.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta,\gamma,\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta,\gamma,\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma)\neq(0,0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma)\neq(0,0)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding 2-spin system defined on <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> with parameters <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> is said to satisfy <em id="Thmtheorem7.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">strong spatial mixing (SSM)</em> with exponential rate <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> if there exists a constant <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,
any feasible partial configurations <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> may be different with <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any vertex <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}-P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}\right|\leq Cr^{-d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></msubsup></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>r</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}-P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}\right|\leq Cr^{-d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem7.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem7.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Here, we denote <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> the set <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\Lambda_{1}\setminus\Lambda_{2})\cup(\Lambda_{2}\setminus\Lambda_{1})\cup\{v\in\Lambda_{1}\cap\Lambda_{2}:\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}(v)\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}(v)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∩</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\Lambda_{1}\setminus\Lambda_{2})\cup(\Lambda_{2}\setminus\Lambda_{1})\cup\{v\in\Lambda_{1}\cap\Lambda_{2}:\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}(v)\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}(v)\}</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., the set on which <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> differ with each other), and <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>v</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> is the shortest distance from <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> to any vertex in <math id="Thmtheorem7.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Note that the SSM property implies the partition function <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z_{G}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>Z</mi><mi>G</mi><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z_{G}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}</annotation></semantics></math> is zero-free on the fixed point <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>γ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}|&lt;\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msubsup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math> for any graph <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and any feasible partial configuration <math id="S2.SS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given a graph <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>E</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> and a vertex <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>,
the SAW tree of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> denoted by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{SAW}}(G,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{SAW}}(G,v)</annotation></semantics></math>, is a tree with the root <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> that
enumerates all self-avoiding paths beginning from <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>.
Additional vertices closing cycles of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> are added as leaves of the tree.
Each vertex in <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to some vertices of <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{SAW}}(G,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{SAW}}(G,v)</annotation></semantics></math>.
A vertex set <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to some <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}\subseteq V_{\text{SAW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo>⊆</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}\subseteq V_{\text{SAW}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and a partial configuration <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}:\Lambda\to\{\pm\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">±</mo><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}:\Lambda\to\{\pm\}</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to a partial configuration <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the set of leaf vertices <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{\text{SAW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{\text{SAW}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> closes a cycle and no vertices in the path between the root <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and the leaf <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> are pinned by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For every vertex in <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
a configuration is imposed to it depending on the orientation of the cycle, where the order of indices of vertices is arbitrarily chosen (see Figure <a href="#S2.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 2.2 Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> for an example).
We denote by <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math> the partial configuration <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}</annotation></semantics></math> together with the imposed configuration on <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>L</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
One can easily check that if <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible in <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is proper to <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is feasible in <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{SAW}}(G,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>T</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>v</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{SAW}}(G,v)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> is proper to <math id="S2.SS2.p1.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mtext>SAW</mtext></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{\text{SAW}}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Here is the key result for the SAW tree construction.</p>
