<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Local dependence of coefficients and a uniform bound on a circle</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem14" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem14.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 14</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem14.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Local dependence of coefficients)<span id="Thmtheorem14.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a complex neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding 2-spin system (defined on <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> specified with the fixed parameters <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, and a variable <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in U</annotation></semantics></math>) is said to satisfy <em id="Thmtheorem14.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">local dependence of coefficients (LDC)</em> (for <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>) if for
any <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,
any feasible partial configurations <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and any vertex <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the functions <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and their corresponding Taylor series <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem14.p1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem15" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 15</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform bound on a circle)<span id="Thmtheorem15.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem15.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a circle <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math> centered at <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>,
and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
The corresponding 2-spin system has a uniform bound <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> on the circle <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> if for any <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, any feasible partial configuration <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, and any vertex <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="Thmtheorem15.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)|\leq M\text{ for all }\lambda\in\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000"> for all </mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)|\leq M\text{ for all }\lambda\in\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now we are ready to establish SSM for a 2-spin system assuming it satisfies LDC and has a uniform bound on a circle.
We first give the following lemma.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(z)</annotation></semantics></math> be two analytic functions on some complex neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Suppose that the Taylor series <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(z)</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>
satisfy <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{k}=b_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{k}=b_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=0,1,\cdots,n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=0,1,\cdots,n</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\in\mathbb{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\in\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also, suppose that there exists an <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that both <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P(z)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P(z)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q(z)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(z)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> on some circle <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><mphantom></mphantom><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\rho&gt;0)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\rho&gt;0)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for every <math id="Thmtheorem16.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
