<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Note that the series <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}a_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(z)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{k\geq 0}b_{k}(z-z_{0})^{k}</annotation></semantics></math> converges to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(z)</annotation></semantics></math> on the closed disk <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}(z_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}(z_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem9" title="Theorem 9 (c.f. Theorem 4.4 in []). ‣ 2.3 Tools from complex analysis ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.
Thus, for every <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}(z_{0}),</annotation></semantics></math> we have</span></p>
