<div id="Thmtheorem17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a complex neighborhood <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>.
If the corresponding 2-spin system satisfies LDC and it has a uniform bound on a circle <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}\subseteq U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}\subseteq U</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,
then for any <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\mathbb{D}_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the 2-spin system exhibits SSM with rate <math id="Thmtheorem17.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\rho/|\lambda|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\rho/|\lambda|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For some arbitrary <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,
some feasible partial configurations <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, and some vertex <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the rational functions <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(\lambda)=P_{G,v}^{\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>. By LDC, these two functions are analytic and the coefficients of the first <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="d_{G}(v,\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\})</annotation></semantics></math> terms in their Taylor series are equal.
Also, by a uniform bound on the circle <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\partial{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\partial{\mathbb{D}_{\rho}}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that
<math id="S3.SS2.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|P(\lambda)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|P(\lambda)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|Q(\lambda)|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|Q(\lambda)|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S3.SS2.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔻</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\partial\mathbb{D}_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the theorem follows directly from Lemma <a href="#Thmtheorem16" title="Lemma 16. ‣ 3.2 Local dependence of coefficients and a uniform bound on a circle ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
