<div id="Thmtheorem19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 19</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If a 2-spin system satisfies point-to-point LDC, then it also satisfies LDC.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">When point-to-point LDC holds, we prove LDC by induction of <math id="S3.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.167em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">When <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.167em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=0,</annotation></semantics></math> the assertion holds immediately. Suppose now that the assertion holds when <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k\geq 0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.167em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k\geq 0,</annotation></semantics></math> then when <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.167em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}|=k+1</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="u\in\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\in\{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}\},</annotation></semantics></math> by point-to-point LDC, the functions
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> are analytic on <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>, and
their corresponding Taylor series <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}a_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum^{\infty}_{i=0}b_{i}\lambda^{i}</annotation></semantics></math> near <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{i}=b_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{i}=b_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq i\leq d(v,u)-1</annotation></semantics></math>; similar equality holds for <math id="S3.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="S3.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{\prime}=\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}},\tau^{\prime}=\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{\prime}=\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}},\tau^{\prime}=\tau_{\Lambda_{2}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math> (recall that <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}}</annotation></semantics></math> means the restriction of <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∖</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{1}\setminus\{u\}</annotation></semantics></math>, if <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u\notin\Lambda_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∉</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u\notin\Lambda_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> then the two partial configurations are the same. ), then we have <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="|\{\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime}\}|=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="false" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.167em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\{\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime}\}|=k</annotation></semantics></math>, hence we can apply the induction hypothesis. Then the conclusion follows since <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,u)\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,u)\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{G}(v,\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime})\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">′</mo></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">τ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{G}(v,\sigma^{\prime}\neq\tau^{\prime})\geq d_{G}(v,\sigma_{\Lambda_{1}}\neq\tau_{\Lambda_{2}}).</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Now, it suffices to prove that point-to-point LDC derives from zero-freeness.
We prove this by establishing a Christoffel-Darboux type identity for 2-spin systems.
By the SAW tree construction and Theorem </span><a href="#Thmtheorem8" title="Theorem 8. ‣ 2.2 Weitz’s algorithm and self-avoiding walk tree ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a><span id="S3.SS3.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we may restrict the graphs to trees.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Before we dig into the general 2-spin system, we first consider a simple case, the hard-core model, the partition function of which is the independence polynomial. This model is the 2-spin system where </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta=0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> For the hard-core model, </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[</span><a href="#bib.bibx31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reg23</a><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">]</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> proved that LDC holds by using a tool called cluster expansion from statistic physics.
Here, we show that it can also be proved by the following Christoffel-Darboux type identity by Gutman </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[</span><a href="#bib.bibx17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gut91</a><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">]</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
For a graph </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a subset </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we use </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G\backslash U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G\backslash U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to denote the graph obtained from </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by deleting all vertices in </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and their adjacent edges (i.e., the subgraph of </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> induced by the vertex set </span><math id="S3.SS3.p6.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V\backslash U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V\backslash U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p6.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 20</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=(V,E)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=(V,E)</annotation></semantics></math> be a tree and <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> be two distinct vertices in <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, for the partition function of the hard-core model on <math id="Thmtheorem20.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
