<div id="S3.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In the following proof and Remark <a href="#Thmremark4" title="Remark 4. ‣ 3.3 Zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we omit the argument <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta,\gamma,\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> of the partition functions for simplicity.
We prove the equality by induction on <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=d(u,v)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=d(u,v)</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda=\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∩</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V(p_{uv})\cap\Lambda=\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>. When <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1,</annotation></semantics></math> <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> are adjacent, Denote <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v_{1},\cdots,v_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">l</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v_{1},\cdots,v_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> neighbors of <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v,v_{l+1},\cdots,v_{n}" display="in