<div id="Thmtheorem23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 23</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Fix complex parameters <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>, a complex neighbourhood <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, and a family of graphs <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>. If
the partition function <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Z</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}_{G,\beta,\gamma}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>
is zero-free on <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\backslash\{0\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\backslash\{0\}</annotation></semantics></math>, then the corresponding 2-spin system satisfies point-to-point LDC on <math id="Thmtheorem23.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S3.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G=(V,E)\in\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, feasible configuration <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}\in\{0,1\}^{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> on some <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda\subseteq V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda\subseteq V</annotation></semantics></math>, and two vertices <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u,v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u,v</annotation></semantics></math> proper to <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider the rational functions <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{+}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></msup></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P_{G,v}^{\sigma_{\Lambda},u^{-}}(\lambda)</annotation></semantics></math>.
One can easily check that
they are analytic on <math id="S3.SS3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">By the SAW tree construction, it suffices to consider the case that <math id="S3.SS3.p15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is a tree. Then, by Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem22" title="Theorem 22. ‣ 3.3 Zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a> and Remark <a href="#Thmremark4" title="Remark 4. ‣ 3.3 Zero-freeness implies local dependence of coefficients ‣ 3 Zero-freeness implies SSM for 𝜆 ‣ From Zero-Freeness to Strong Spatial Mixing viaa Christoffel-Darboux Type Identity" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>,</span></p>
