<div id="Thmtheorem30" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem30.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 30</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem30.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Uniform bound on a circle centered at <math id="Thmtheorem30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem30.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem30.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem30.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> be
a family of graphs, <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> be quasi-neighborhoods of some <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{0},\lambda_{0}{&gt;0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{0},\lambda_{0}{&gt;0}</annotation></semantics></math> respectively where <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\notin U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∉</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\notin U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> be a neighborhood of <math id="Thmtheorem30.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/U_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/U_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
