<p id="S5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where <math id="S5.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of <math id="S5.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(+,+)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">+</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(+,+)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(-,-)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">,</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(-,-)</annotation></semantics></math> edges in the subgraph of <math id="S5.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> induced by <math id="S5.p5.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math> conditioning on <math id="S5.p5.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\Lambda}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\Lambda}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{2}=\sum_{w\in\Lambda\atop\sigma_{\Lambda}(w)=-}|N(w)\cap(V\backslash\Lambda)|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" linethickness="0pt" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">=</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></mrow></mfrac></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∩</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{2}=\sum_{w\in\Lambda\atop\sigma_{\Lambda}(w)=-}|N(w)\cap(V\backslash\Lambda)|</annotation></semantics></math>.
Note that <math id="S5.p5.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S5.p5.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{v}\neq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≠</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{v}\neq 0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S5.p5.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">v</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in V</annotation></semantics></math>.
Also since the degree of vertices in <math id="S5.p5.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math> is at most <math id="S5.p5.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, for every <math id="S5.p5.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\in V\backslash\Lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">V</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">\</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\in V\backslash\Lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
